{
  "abstract": "A pure-Init Lean 4.35.0 formalization (zero Mathlib dependencies, zero SAT certificates) disproving the Section 5 conjecture of Fanelli and Moscardelli (ECAI 2025, hal-05368668; google-deepmind/formal-conjectures FanelliMoscardelli.stability_threshold_tight). Proves via an elementary 9-lemma structural proof that for every integer m >= 3, every complete strict preference profile on N = 2m + 1 agents admits an m-stable matching, giving K(2m + 1) <= m < ceil((2m + 1)/2) and refuting stability_threshold_tight using only the three standard Lean axioms [propext, Quot.sound, Classical.choice].",
